# defconfigs/qemu-aarch64.config — Aarch64 / QEMU virt / Edge profile
#
# Target: QEMU virt aarch64 (cortex-a72 simulation), Phase 2 multi-arch dev.
#         The `crates/aarch64-hello` standalone demonstrates EL2→EL1→GICv3→
#         MMU→EL0 chain.  Full robot kernel loop on aarch64 is deferred to
#         Phase 3 hardware bring-up (no physical aarch64 SBC in scope).
#
# Memory budget (rough):
#   Static tables (RFC-0023 edge, aarch64 stack sizes larger): ~4-5 MiB
#   Kernel heap (KERNEL_HEAP_SIZE = 32768 KiB): 32 MiB
#   Lazy user stacks (MAX_TASKS=64 × 32 KiB NEON save): ~2 MiB physical
#   Total worst-case: ~38-40 MiB  (well within QEMU 256 MiB RAM)
#
# Notable vs. RISC-V edge defaults:
#   ARCH=AARCH64 (FP_NEON, USER_STACK_SIZE_KB=32, KERNEL_STACK_SIZE_KB=32)
#   BOARD=QEMU, PROFILE=EDGE.
#   DRV_CSI=n       — no JH7110/K1 CSI block in aarch64 QEMU; mock driver absent.
#   DRV_VIRTIO_BLK_NET=n — aarch64 QEMU boot flow not yet wired to VirtIO init.
#   DRV_MACB_ETHERNET=n  — MACB is RISC-V VF2-only; stays n everywhere else anyway.
#   USB drivers: already default n (no BOARD_VF2/K1 trigger).
#
# Build status: `cargo build` for full kernel NOT supported yet on aarch64.
#   The `aarch64-unknown-none-softfloat` target builds crates/aarch64-hello only.
#   Run `make olddefconfig` to validate; skip cargo build in C5 verification.
#
# Regenerate with:  make defconfig-qemu-aarch64 && make savedefconfig
CONFIG_ARCH_AARCH64=y
# CONFIG_DRV_CSI is not set
# CONFIG_DRV_VIRTIO_BLK_NET is not set
